The main reason is automation.

Imagine you are a Linux administrator managing 100 Linux servers.

You need to check:

Disk space
CPU
Memory
Running services
Logs
Backup status

Doing this manually on every server would take a lot of time.

Instead, you can create a script that performs these checks automatically.

For example:

#!/bin/bash

echo "Disk:"
df -h

echo "Memory:"
free -h

echo "Uptime:"
uptime

Now one command:

./server_check.sh

can perform multiple checks.

=> In simple words:

Without scripting:

You → Manually do 10 tasks

With scripting:

You → Run 1 script → 10 tasks happen automatically.
